  <main class="detail-main refined-utility" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Dentistry in the context of your whole health</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Our philosophy</p><h1>Dentistry in the context of your whole health</h1><p class="detail-lead">At Raina Dental Care, the conversation can include your oral health, history, goals and material preferences. Excellent dentistry still begins with a careful diagnosis and an evidence-informed treatment plan.</p></div></div>
<section class="wrap editorial-single"><div class="section-intro-narrow"><p class="eyebrow">What we mean</p><h2>Thoughtful care is more than a treatment.</h2><p class="intro-large">Biological dentistry is a philosophy of considering oral health in the wider context of a patient’s wellbeing, with special attention to prevention, patient education and material choices.</p><p>It does not remove the need for clinical examinations, imaging when indicated, conventional restorative treatment or medical referral. We believe that better decisions come from understanding what is known, what remains uncertain and what matters to the individual patient.</p></div><div class="explain-list"><article class="explain-block"><span class="explain-index">01</span><div><h3>Listen before recommending</h3><p>An appointment begins with your concerns and relevant medical and dental history. Goals, anxiety and personal preferences help shape the discussion.</p></div></article><article class="explain-block"><span class="explain-index">02</span><div><h3>Consider dental materials carefully</h3><p>We can talk about the materials used in restorations, potential sensitivities and the evidence and tradeoffs behind different choices.</p></div></article><article class="explain-block"><span class="explain-index">03</span><div><h3>Balance prevention with treatment</h3><p>Good oral hygiene and preventive care matter; when a tooth needs treatment, we explain the practical options and why they are recommended.</p></div></article><article class="explain-block"><span class="explain-index">04</span><div><h3>Be measured about amalgam removal</h3><p>When an existing filling needs replacement, protective protocols may be discussed. Intact amalgam does not routinely need to be removed solely to reduce mercury exposure.</p></div></article></div><div class="editorial-faq"><h2>What do “mercury-free” and “mercury-safe” mean?</h2><p>These phrases are commonly used by dental practices to describe avoiding new mercury-containing amalgam restorations and using specific safety precautions when existing amalgam must be removed. They are not claims that removing a filling treats systemic illness.</p></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/care/smart/">Explore SMART removal <svg aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="/care/team/">Meet our dentists <svg aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></section><section class="end-cta"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Raina Dental Care</p><h2>Ready for a conversation?</h2><p>Reach our Naperville team to talk about your next visit.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/care/appointments/">Schedule a visit <svg aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="tel:+16303814021">Call (630) 381-4021 <svg aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></div></div></section></main>
